From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] venus: hide workgroup zero-init on MoltenVK

What: vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2 reports shaderZeroInitializeWorkgroupMemory
as unsupported when the host driver is MoltenVK.

Why: MoltenVK 1.4.2 (its SPIRV-Cross) compiles a zero-initialized workgroup
variable into a loop over gl_WorkGroupSize but never declares it when the
shader sets its size with LocalSize. Metal then refuses the shader ("use of
undeclared identifier 'gl_WorkGroupSize'"), vkCreateComputePipelines fails,
and the guest's next vkCmdBindPipeline names an object vkr never created:
the whole context is lost. WebGPU in Firefox (wgpu) zero-initializes all
workgroup memory, so every WebGPU compute shader with workgroup memory took
Firefox down. Without the feature, wgpu (and Dawn, ANGLE) zero the memory
in the shader themselves. SPIRV-Cross main declares gl_WorkGroupSize from
LocalSize for this case; drop the patch once MoltenVK ships that.

The driver is recognised by its driverID, asked for whenever the device
offers it (Vulkan 1.2, or VK_KHR_driver_properties): a guest instance
created for Vulkan 1.1 (Chrome's Dawn) must get the same answer as a 1.3
one (Firefox). MoltenVK reports the instance's version as the device's, so
a version check alone skipped Dawn.

Upstream: MoltenVK/SPIRV-Cross bug, fixed upstream in SPIRV-Cross; this
workaround is OmacVM-only (not for virglrenderer upstream).
Test: Firefox WebGPU compute with var<workgroup> (scratch wgtest.js wgmem,
matmul.js) runs; before, Firefox died at the first dispatch. Chrome
(Dawn, Vulkan 1.1 instance) runs the same matmul; when this check used
the instance's version, Dawn still saw the feature and lost its context.

--- a/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_physical_device.c
@@ -704,6 +704,38 @@
 
    vn_replace_vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2_args_handle(args);
    vk->GetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2(args->physicalDevice, args->pFeatures);
+
+   /* MoltenVK 1.4.2's SPIRV-Cross turns zero-initialized workgroup variables
+    * into a loop over gl_WorkGroupSize without declaring it when the shader
+    * sets its size with LocalSize: such compute pipelines fail to compile
+    * (WebGPU in Firefox and Chrome zero-initializes all workgroup memory).
+    * Without the feature, apps zero the memory themselves. MoltenVK reports
+    * the instance's version as the device's (1.1 for Chrome's Dawn), so look
+    * for the extension too.
+    */
+   bool has_driver_props = physical_dev->api_version >= VK_API_VERSION_1_2;
+   for (uint32_t i = 0; !has_driver_props && i < physical_dev->extension_count; i++)
+      has_driver_props = !strcmp(physical_dev->extensions[i].extensionName,
+                                 VK_KHR_DRIVER_PROPERTIES_EXTENSION_NAME);
+   if (!has_driver_props)
+      return;
+   VkPhysicalDeviceDriverProperties driver_props = {
+      .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_DRIVER_PROPERTIES,
+   };
+   VkPhysicalDeviceProperties2 props2 = {
+      .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_PROPERTIES_2,
+      .pNext = &driver_props,
+   };
+   vk->GetPhysicalDeviceProperties2(args->physicalDevice, &props2);
+   if (driver_props.driverID != VK_DRIVER_ID_MOLTENVK)
+      return;
+   for (VkBaseOutStructure *s = (VkBaseOutStructure *)args->pFeatures; s; s = s->pNext) {
+      if (s->sType == VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_VULKAN_1_3_FEATURES)
+         ((VkPhysicalDeviceVulkan13Features *)s)->shaderZeroInitializeWorkgroupMemory = VK_FALSE;
+      else if (s->sType == VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_ZERO_INITIALIZE_WORKGROUP_MEMORY_FEATURES)
+         ((VkPhysicalDeviceZeroInitializeWorkgroupMemoryFeatures *)s)
+            ->shaderZeroInitializeWorkgroupMemory = VK_FALSE;
+   }
 }
 
 static void
